<h2 id="%f0%9f%94%8e-key-cream-cheese-rotisserie-chicken-enchilada-recipe-takeaways"   class="wp-block-heading" >🔎 Key Cream Cheese Rotisserie Chicken Enchilada Recipe Takeaways</h2>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Combining rotisserie chicken with cream cheese is a shortcut to pure comfort food. Delicious.</li>



<li>Unlike standard sour cream enchiladas, the addition of cream cheese creates a much thicker, richer filling that holds its shape perfectly inside the tortillas.</li>



<li>The use of RoTel <em>(diced tomatoes and green chiles)</em> provides a necessary acidic note that cuts through the heavy dairy, ensuring the dish is flavorful rather than just heavy.</li>



<li>A 50/50 blend of Pepper Jack and Sharp Cheddar gives you the best of both worlds: a spicy, gooey melt and a sharp, golden crust.</li>



<li>This recipe acts as a blank canvas or starting point. You can easily bulk it up with black beans or corn, or swap the red sauce for green to change the entire flavor profile.</li>



<li>Enchiladas are sturdy and reheat beautifully, making them an ideal candidate for make-ahead freezer meals or a week of meal-prepped delicious lunches.</li>
</ul>



<h2 id="%f0%9f%a5%98-ingredients"   class="wp-block-heading" >🥘 Ingredients</h2>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1800" data-pin-nopin="true" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%201800'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Cream cheese rotisserie chicken enchiladas recipe ingredients measured out and labeled, ready to mix and assemble." class="wp-image-195198" data-lazy-srcset="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-labeled-ingredients.jpg 1200w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-labeled-ingredients-200x300.jpg 200w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-labeled-ingredients-400x600.jpg 400w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-labeled-ingredients-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-labeled-ingredients-720x1080.jpg 720w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-labeled-ingredients-360x540.jpg 360w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-labeled-ingredients-180x270.jpg 180w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-labeled-ingredients-150x225.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-labeled-ingredients.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1800" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-labeled-ingredients.jpg" alt="Cream cheese rotisserie chicken enchiladas recipe ingredients measured out and labeled, ready to mix and assemble." class="wp-image-195198" srcset="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-labeled-ingredients.jpg 1200w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-labeled-ingredients-200x300.jpg 200w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-labeled-ingredients-400x600.jpg 400w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-labeled-ingredients-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-labeled-ingredients-720x1080.jpg 720w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-labeled-ingredients-360x540.jpg 360w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-labeled-ingredients-180x270.jpg 180w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-labeled-ingredients-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Rotisserie Chicken</strong> - The ultimate kitchen cheat for flavor and convenience. Using pre-cooked chicken ensures the meat is tender and juicy, having already soaked up seasonings from the roasting process. If you have a Costco near you, I'm sure you grab plenty of deli rotisserie chicken!</li>



<li><strong>Cream Cheese</strong> - The star of the show! It provides a rich, velvety texture that binds the filling together and creates a luxurious contrast to the spicy sauce. I recommend full-fat cream cheese for maximum creaminess.</li>



<li><strong>Sour Cream <em>(or Greek yogurt)</em></strong> - Adds a necessary tang to cut through the richness of the cheeses. It also keeps the filling moist during the baking process.</li>



<li><strong>RoTel Diced Tomatoes <em>(with green chiles)</em></strong> - These add a bright, acidic pop and a hint of zesty heat. They break up the "creaminess" with little bursts of texture. You can also use a 10 ounce can of diced tomatoes + a 4 ounce can of diced green chiles or jalapenos.</li>



<li><strong>Red Enchilada Sauce</strong> - This provides the earthy, smoky base that defines the dish. It coats the tortillas and seeps into the edges for that classic enchilada finish. Swap for green enchilada sauce for a tasty variation.</li>



<li><strong>Pepper Jack Cheese</strong> - Known for its superior meltability, this adds a subtle kick of heat within the filling. Colby-Jack or Monterey Jack can also be used.</li>



<li><strong>Cheddar Cheese <em>(or fiesta Mexican-blend)</em></strong> - Provides that sharp, classic flavor and creates a beautiful, golden-brown crust on top when baked.</li>



<li><strong>Flour Tortillas</strong> - These are soft and sturdy, making them perfect for holding a heavy cream cheese filling without tearing. They soak up the sauce beautifully while remaining tender.</li>



<li><strong>Taco Seasoning</strong> - This deepens the flavor profile, adding notes of cumin, chili powder, and garlic to the chicken so every bite is flavorfully seasoned.</li>



<li><strong>Fresh Cilantro</strong> - A final garnish that adds a pop of color and a fresh, herbal finish to balance the savory weight of the cheese. Use green onions or parsley if desired.</li>
</ul>



<div class="wp-block-group is-style-group-asterisk"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Be sure to see the <em><strong>free printable recipe card below</strong></em> for ingredients, exact amounts &amp; instructions with tips!</p>
</div></div>



<div style="background-color: #fdfdfd; border: 2px solid #723d7c; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Oxygen-Sans, Ubuntu, Cantarell, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif;">
<h2 id="%f0%9f%a5%a3-flavor-texture-stir-ins"   style="margin-top: 0; color: #333;">🥣 Flavor & Texture Stir-Ins</h2>
<p>One of the best things about these <strong>cream cheese rotisserie chicken enchiladas</strong> is they're a blank canvas and super easy to customize! Stir in one or two of these extras to add layers of flavor, add a variety of textures to your filling, or bulk up and spread the filling out to make 2 batches of enchilada dinners:</p>

<div style="overflow-x: auto;">
    <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 15px;">
        <thead>
            <tr style="background-color: #723d7c; color: #ffffff; text-align: left;">
                <th style="padding: 12px; border: 1px solid #723d7c;">Stir-In Idea</th>
                <th style="padding: 12px; border: 1px solid #723d7c;">Flavor Profile</th>
                <th style="padding: 12px; border: 1px solid #723d7c;">Why it Works</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;"><strong>Black Beans</strong></td>
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;">Earthy & Hearty</td>
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;">Adds a boost of protein and a nice contrast to the creamy cheese.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="background-color: #f9f9f9;">
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;"><strong>Sweet Corn</strong></td>
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;">Sweet & Crisp</td>
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;">Provides a subtle "pop" of texture that cuts through the richness.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;"><strong>Diced Green Chiles</strong></td>
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;">Zesty & Mild</td>
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;">Adds extra "zip" and flavor without overwhelming heat.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="background-color: #f9f9f9;">
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;"><strong>Sautéed Aromatics</strong></td>
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;">Savory & Deep</td>
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;">Softened onions and garlic elevate the rotisserie chicken instantly.</td>
            </tr>
             <tr>
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;"><strong>Pickled Jalapeños</strong></td>
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;">Tangy & Spicy</td>
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;">The vinegar-based tang balances the heavy cream cheese beautifully.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="background-color: #f9f9f9;">
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;"><strong>Chipotle in Adobo</strong></td>
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;">Smoky & Bold</td>
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;">A teaspoon of sauce adds a deep heat that pairs with the red sauce.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;"><strong>Green Onions</strong></td>
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;">Fresh & Sharp</td>
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;">Stir in at the end for a fresh bite within the melted filling.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="background-color: #f9f9f9;">
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;"><strong>Bell Peppers</strong></td>
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;">Sweet & Vibrant</td>
                <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #ddd;">Sautéed peppers add color and a delicious "fajita-style" vibe.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>
<p style="margin-top: 15px; font-style: italic;"><strong>💡 Tip:</strong> If you're adding wet ingredients like canned beans or extra chiles, make sure they are <strong>very well-drained</strong>. You want to keep that filling thick and creamy, not watery!</p>
</div>



<h2 id="%f0%9f%94%aa-how-to-make-cream-cheese-rotisserie-chicken-enchiladas"   class="wp-block-heading" >🔪 How To Make Cream Cheese Rotisserie Chicken Enchiladas</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Grab a mixing bowl, measuring utensils, a spatula or spoon to stir your filling together with, a cheese grater, and a <strong>9x13 baking dish</strong> to get started.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This hearty dinner recipe yields 8 servings. Serve with a side of my <strong><a href="https://bakeitwithlove.com/restaurant-style-mexican-rice-recipe/" type="post" id="5190">restaurant-style Mexican rice</a></strong>, <strong><a href="https://bakeitwithlove.com/healthy-refried-black-beans/" type="post" id="6944">refried black beans</a></strong>, and <strong><a href="https://bakeitwithlove.com/easy-homemade-roasted-salsa-roja/" type="post" id="5877">salsa roja</a></strong> or <strong><a href="https://bakeitwithlove.com/pico-de-gallo-recipe/" type="post" id="5157">pico de gallo</a></strong>.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-prep-amp-mix-the-filling">Prep &amp; Mix The Filling</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Preheat and prep baking dish.</strong> Set your oven to 350°F <em>(175°C/Gas Mark 4)</em> and lightly grease a 9x13 baking pan. Pour ½ cup of the enchilada sauce into the bottom of the dish.</p>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-8f761849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="600" height="900" data-pin-nopin="true" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20600%20900'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Cream cheese rotisserie chicken enchiladas process photo 1 combining the softened cream cheese, sour cream, and taco seasoning." class="wp-image-195197" data-lazy-srcset="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process1.jpg 600w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process1-200x300.jpg 200w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process1-400x600.jpg 400w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process1-360x540.jpg 360w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process1-180x270.jpg 180w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process1-150x225.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px" data-lazy-src="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process1.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="600" height="900" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process1.jpg" alt="Cream cheese rotisserie chicken enchiladas process photo 1 combining the softened cream cheese, sour cream, and taco seasoning." class="wp-image-195197" srcset="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process1.jpg 600w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process1-200x300.jpg 200w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process1-400x600.jpg 400w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process1-360x540.jpg 360w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process1-180x270.jpg 180w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process1-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px" /></noscript></figure>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="600" height="900" data-pin-nopin="true" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20600%20900'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Cream cheese rotisserie chicken enchiladas process photo 2 adding the shredded rotisserie chicken meat, cheeses, and drained RoTel tomatoes with diced chiles." class="wp-image-195196" data-lazy-srcset="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process2.jpg 600w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process2-200x300.jpg 200w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process2-400x600.jpg 400w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process2-360x540.jpg 360w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process2-180x270.jpg 180w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process2-150x225.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px" data-lazy-src="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process2.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="600" height="900" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process2.jpg" alt="Cream cheese rotisserie chicken enchiladas process photo 2 adding the shredded rotisserie chicken meat, cheeses, and drained RoTel tomatoes with diced chiles." class="wp-image-195196" srcset="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process2.jpg 600w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process2-200x300.jpg 200w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process2-400x600.jpg 400w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process2-360x540.jpg 360w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process2-180x270.jpg 180w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process2-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px" /></noscript></figure>
</div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Combine cream cheese and seasoning.</strong> In a large mixing bowl, stir the softened 8 ounce brick of cream cheese and ¼&nbsp;cup&nbsp;sour cream until creamy and spreadable. Add the 1½&nbsp;teaspoons of&nbsp;<strong><a href="https://bakeitwithlove.com/taco-seasoning-mix-recipe/">taco seasoning</a></strong> or <strong><a href="https://bakeitwithlove.com/chicken-taco-seasoning/">chicken taco seasoning</a></strong> <em>(photo 1)</em> then stir until it's evenly distributed in the cream cheese mixture.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Mix in chicken, tomatoes, and cheese.</strong> Stir in 2 pounds or 4 cups of shredded rotisserie chicken meat, the drained 10 ounce can of Rotel diced tomatoes with green chiles, and ½ cup shredded pepper jack cheese along with ½ cup of the shredded cheddar cheese <em>(photo 2)</em>. Combine until well coated with the seasoned mixture <em>(photo 3)</em>.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-assemble-bake-amp-serve">Assemble, Bake &amp; Serve</h3>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-8f761849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="600" height="900" data-pin-nopin="true" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20600%20900'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Cream cheese rotisserie chicken enchiladas process photo 3 fully combined creamy chicken mixture." class="wp-image-195195" data-lazy-srcset="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process3.jpg 600w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process3-200x300.jpg 200w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process3-400x600.jpg 400w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process3-360x540.jpg 360w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process3-180x270.jpg 180w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process3-150x225.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px" data-lazy-src="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process3.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="600" height="900" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process3.jpg" alt="Cream cheese rotisserie chicken enchiladas process photo 3 fully combined creamy chicken mixture." class="wp-image-195195" srcset="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process3.jpg 600w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process3-200x300.jpg 200w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process3-400x600.jpg 400w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process3-360x540.jpg 360w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process3-180x270.jpg 180w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process3-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px" /></noscript></figure>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="600" height="900" data-pin-nopin="true" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20600%20900'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Cream cheese rotisserie chicken enchiladas process photo 4 filling the center of a flour tortilla with the chicken mixture to roll up for the enchiladas." class="wp-image-195194" data-lazy-srcset="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process4.jpg 600w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process4-200x300.jpg 200w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process4-400x600.jpg 400w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process4-360x540.jpg 360w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process4-180x270.jpg 180w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process4-150x225.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px" data-lazy-src="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process4.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="600" height="900" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process4.jpg" alt="Cream cheese rotisserie chicken enchiladas process photo 4 filling the center of a flour tortilla with the chicken mixture to roll up for the enchiladas." class="wp-image-195194" srcset="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process4.jpg 600w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process4-200x300.jpg 200w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process4-400x600.jpg 400w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process4-360x540.jpg 360w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process4-180x270.jpg 180w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process4-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px" /></noscript></figure>
</div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Fill each tortilla.</strong> Start with a flat 8-inch flour tortilla, and add a ½ cup of the chicken mixture in a line down the center of each tortilla <em>(photo 4)</em>. Roll and place seam-side down in your prepared dish. Repeat until all of the tortillas are filled.</p>



<div class="wp-block-group is-style-group-question"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Do you roll only? Or do you tuck your enchiladas in like a burrito? I like mine either way! I also fill my dish with any extra filling I have left over.</p>
</div></div>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-8f761849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="600" height="900" data-pin-nopin="true" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20600%20900'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Cream cheese rotisserie chicken enchiladas process photo 5 rolled enchiladas topped with sauce and cheese." class="wp-image-195193" data-lazy-srcset="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process5.jpg 600w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process5-200x300.jpg 200w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process5-400x600.jpg 400w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process5-360x540.jpg 360w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process5-180x270.jpg 180w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process5-150x225.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px" data-lazy-src="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process5.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="600" height="900" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process5.jpg" alt="Cream cheese rotisserie chicken enchiladas process photo 5 rolled enchiladas topped with sauce and cheese." class="wp-image-195193" srcset="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process5.jpg 600w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process5-200x300.jpg 200w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process5-400x600.jpg 400w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process5-360x540.jpg 360w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process5-180x270.jpg 180w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process5-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px" /></noscript></figure>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="600" height="900" data-pin-nopin="true" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20600%20900'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Cream cheese rotisserie chicken enchiladas process photo 6 baked enchiladas ready to serve while hot." class="wp-image-195192" data-lazy-srcset="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process6.jpg 600w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process6-200x300.jpg 200w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process6-400x600.jpg 400w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process6-360x540.jpg 360w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process6-180x270.jpg 180w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process6-150x225.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px" data-lazy-src="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process6.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="600" height="900" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process6.jpg" alt="Cream cheese rotisserie chicken enchiladas process photo 6 baked enchiladas ready to serve while hot." class="wp-image-195192" srcset="https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process6.jpg 600w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process6-200x300.jpg 200w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process6-400x600.jpg 400w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process6-360x540.jpg 360w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process6-180x270.jpg 180w, https://bakeitwithlove.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Cream-Cheese-Rotisserie-Chicken-Enchiladas-process6-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px" /></noscript></figure>
</div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Sauce and top with cheese.</strong> Pour the remaining enchilada sauce over the dish of enchiladas then sprinkle with the remaining cheddar and pepper jack cheeses on top of the enchiladas <em>(photo 5)</em>.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Bake until melted and bubbling.</strong> Bake in the center of your preheated oven for 25-30 minutes. The sauce should be hot and bubbling around the edges and the cheese should be fully melted <em>(photo 6)</em>. For a golden brown and slightly crisped top, broil on high for an extra 2-3 minutes before removing from the oven.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Garnish and serve.</strong> Portion out and serve while hot, topped with fresh chopped cilantro, green onions <em>(scallions)</em>, or parsley.</p>



