<div id="recipe-189346-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-189346-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="189346"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-center wprm-header-decoration-line wprm-header-has-actions" style="padding: 13px 0px;"><div class="wprm-decoration-line" style="border-color: #f7ebff;"></div>Instructions<div class="wprm-decoration-line" style="border-color: #f7ebff;"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class="wprm-spacer" style="height: 13px;"></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">Prep &amp; Mix The Filling</h4><ul style="--wprm-advanced-list-background: #723d7c;" class="wprm-advanced-list wprm-advanced-list-reset wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-189346-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: none;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Preheat your oven to 350°F <em>(175°C/Gas Mark 4)</em> and lightly grease a 9x13 baking dish. Spread a ½ cup of enchilada sauce across the bottom of the pan in a thin layer.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-189346-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: none;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Shred the <span class="wprm-inline-ingredient wprm-inline-ingredient-189346-0 wprm-block-text-bold" data-both-units="0">2 lbs&#32;rotisserie chicken meat</span>. In a large bowl, blend the softened <span class="wprm-inline-ingredient wprm-inline-ingredient-189346-1 wprm-block-text-bold" data-both-units="0">8 oz&#32;cream cheese</span>, <span class="wprm-inline-ingredient wprm-inline-ingredient-189346-2 wprm-block-text-bold" data-both-units="0">¼ cup&#32;sour cream</span>, and <span class="wprm-inline-ingredient wprm-inline-ingredient-189346-8 wprm-block-text-bold" data-both-units="0">1½ tsp&#32;taco seasoning</span> until smooth and combined.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-189346-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: none;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Stir in the shredded rotisserie chicken, drained <span class="wprm-inline-ingredient wprm-inline-ingredient-189346-3 wprm-block-text-bold" data-both-units="0">10 oz&#32;RoTel diced tomatoes with green chilies</span>, and the first half of the shredded <span class="wprm-inline-ingredient wprm-inline-ingredient-189346-5 wprm-block-text-bold" data-both-units="0">1 cup&#32;pepper jack cheese</span> and 1 cup <span class="wprm-inline-ingredient wprm-inline-ingredient-189346-6 wprm-block-text-bold" data-both-units="0">1 cup&#32;cheddar cheese</span> then mix until the chicken is well coated.</span></div></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">Assemble Enchiladas &amp; Bake</h4><ul style="--wprm-advanced-list-background: #723d7c;" class="wprm-advanced-list wprm-advanced-list-reset wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-189346-step-1-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: none;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Spoon the chicken mixture down the center of each of the <span class="wprm-inline-ingredient wprm-inline-ingredient-189346-7 wprm-block-text-bold" data-both-units="0">8 8-inch&#32;flour tortillas</span>. Roll them tightly and place them seam-side down in the prepared baking dish.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-189346-step-1-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: none;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Pour the remaining <span class="wprm-inline-ingredient wprm-inline-ingredient-189346-4 wprm-block-text-bold" data-both-units="0">28 oz&#32;red enchilada sauce</span> over the assembled enchiladas and sprinkle with the rest of the shredded cheese.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-189346-step-1-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: none;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Bake until the sauce is hot and bubbling and the cheese has completely melted. For a golden finish, broil for a few minutes at the end.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-189346-step-1-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: none;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Remove from the oven, serve immediately garnished with fresh <span class="wprm-inline-ingredient wprm-inline-ingredient-189346-9 wprm-block-text-bold" data-both-units="0">1 bunch&#32;cilantro</span>, green onions, or parsley.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>


<div id="recipe-189346-notes" class="wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-center wprm-header-decoration-line" style=""><div class="wprm-decoration-line" style="border-color: #f7ebff;"></div>Notes<div class="wprm-decoration-line" style="border-color: #f7ebff;"></div></h3><div class="wprm-recipe-notes"><ul>
<li>Ensure that cream cheese is at room temperature for a smooth filling. In a pinch, microwave the unwrapped brick for 15-20 seconds on low power.</li>
<li>Microwave tortillas for 15 seconds wrapped in a damp paper towel to make them easier to roll without cracking.</li>
<li>Conversion: 8 ounces = 1 cup of enchilada sauce.</li>
<li>Use only a thin layer of sauce in the bottom of the dish to prevent the tortillas from becoming mushy or soggy on the bottoms.</li>
<li>Shred rotisserie chicken while it's still warm for the best texture; discard skin and fat for a creamier filling.</li>
<li>Freshly shredded cheese melts much better than pre-packaged varieties, which contain anti-caking agents.</li>
<li>Use 'Mild' or 'Hot' RoTel and enchilada sauce to control the spice level. Add a dash of cayenne or extra green chiles for more heat.</li>
<li>To store: Transfer cooled leftovers to an airtight container and keep in the fridge for up to 3-4 days.</li>
<li>To freeze: Keep baked leftovers in a freezer storage container for up to 2-3 months. Thaw before reheating.</li>
</ul></div></div>


<div id="recipe-189346-nutrition" class="wprm-nutrition-label-shortcode-container"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-nutrition-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-center wprm-header-decoration-line" style=""><div class="wprm-decoration-line" style="border-color: #f7ebff;"></div>Nutrition<div class="wprm-decoration-line" style="border-color: #f7ebff;"></div></h3><div class="wprm-nutrition-label-container wprm-nutrition-label-container-simple wprm-block-text-normal" style="text-align: center;"><span class="wprm-nutrition-label-text-nutrition-container wprm-nutrition-label-text-nutrition-container-calories"><span class="wprm-nutrition-label-text-nutrition-label  wprm-block-text-normal" style="color: #000000">Calories: </span><span class="wprm-nutrition-label-text-nutrition-value" style="color: #333333">594</span><span class="wprm-nutrition-label-text-nutrition-unit" style="color: #333333">kcal</span><span class="wprm-nutrition-label-text-nutrition-daily" style="color: #333333"> (30%)</span></span><span style="color: #000000"> | </span><span class="wprm-nutrition-label-text-nutrition-container wprm-nutrition-label-text-nutrition-container-carbohydrates"><span class="wprm-nutrition-label-text-nutrition-label  wprm-block-text-normal" style="color: #000000">Carbohydrates: </span><span class="wprm-nutrition-label-text-nutrition-value" style="color: #333333">37</span><span class="wprm-nutrition-label-text-nutrition-unit" style="color: #333333">g</span><span class="wprm-nutrition-label-text-nutrition-daily" style="color: #333333"> (12%)</span></span><span style="color: #000000"> | </span><span class="wprm-nutrition-label-text-nutrition-container wprm-nutrition-label-text-nutrition-container-protein"><span class="wprm-nutrition-label-text-nutrition-label  wprm-block-text-normal" style="color: #000000">Protein: </span><span class="wprm-nutrition-label-text-nutrition-value" style="color: #333333">48</span><span class="wprm-nutrition-label-text-nutrition-unit" style="c